SSH in.
    root@ubuntu:~$ ssh bandit10@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220

The password for the next level is stored in the file data.txt, which contains base64 encoded data.

lets check it
    bandit10@bandit:~$ ls
    data.txt
    bandit10@bandit:~$ cat data.txt 
    VGhlIHBhc3N3b3JkIGlzIHBZZk9ZNkh3VXNEajVyTDlVdnloVTdNQ212OHZONVJvCg==

The data.txt file is encoded in base64. To get the original we must decode it.
This is done with a simple command of base64 -d
    bandit10@bandit:~$ base64 -d data.txt 
    The password is pYfOY6HwUsDj5rL9UvyhU7MCmv8vN5Ro
